// The special functions of the package: the layer of pairs of doubles, the
// input checks and the polynomial helpers.
//
// Every call returns the result first and a fault code last. A fault
// gives NaN as the result. The checks run in one order: NaN, infinity,
// domain, pole. The result of a call that cannot fit gives the overflow
// code. Every loop has a fixed bound.
//
// The layer of pairs of doubles holds about 30 digits. The log gamma
// terms of the beta cancel, so the incomplete calls need the layer. The
// tables are Chebyshev fits and series terms. The generator under test/
// wrote the numbers from exact arithmetic at 60 to 140 digits.
